      <h2>Why sourcing the right lotion pump decides your bottle's fate</h2>
      <p>
        A lotion pump looks like a 6-gram piece of plastic. In reality it is the single
        highest-failure component on a personal care bottle: a clogged pump, a leaking dip tube, or a
        1.2 mL dose where the formulator specified 0.8 mL — any one of these will trigger a consumer
        return, a retail chargeback, or a relabel cycle that costs more than the entire pump order.
      </p>
      <p>
        This guide is written for B2B buyers who need to make that decision once and get it right. We
        pull spec data from the lotion pump SKUs currently in production at our Cixi, Ningbo factory
        and tell you exactly what we can deliver — MOQ, lead time, material grades, neck sizes,
        finish options — with verifiable numbers in every section instead of generic adjectives. By
        the end you will know which neck size fits your bottle line, which closure finish suits your
        brand positioning, what lead time and MOQ you should hold suppliers to, and how to spec a
        custom pump without overpaying for tooling.
      </p>

