      <ul>
        {nav.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>

      <h2>How a lotion pump works — anatomy of a 6-gram component</h2>
      <p>
        A standard lotion pump has 7 functional parts: <strong
          >actuator (head), closure ring, gasket, piston, spring, dip tube and stem</strong
        >. When the user pushes the actuator, the piston compresses the spring and pushes air out of
        the chamber; when released, the spring expands and the resulting vacuum draws lotion up the
        dip tube. A check ball at the base of the chamber prevents backflow.
      </p>
      <p>
        Three things have to be right for this mechanism to deliver consistent performance across a
        24-month shelf life:
      </p>
    </div>

