      <p><strong>Two practical notes from production:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          For alcohol-based disinfectants (60%+ ethanol): use PP-only construction with no metal
          spring. Alcohol attacks unprotected steel within 6 months of contact; even stainless
          springs may corrode if the spring touches the formula. We can spec an alcohol-rated SKU
          with a fully encapsulated piston that isolates the spring from product contact.
        </li>
        <li>
          For high-viscosity products (&gt;8,000 cP): standard piston geometry won't pull viscous
          lotion at full stroke. Either step up to a 2.0 mL+ dose pump (longer stroke, more chamber
          volume) or move to a treatment-pump-style geometry. We can recommend an SKU after viscosity
          testing on a 50 mL formula sample.
        </li>
